From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: HDR only in full screen (experimental)

What: the app's switch hdrFullScreenOnly (defaults key; QEMU runs as the
app and watches it with KVO, so a running VM follows it at once;
OMACVM_HDR_FULL_SCREEN_ONLY=1 for a QEMU not started as the app), only
with HDR at this start. On, the main output's entry in the layout on
OmacVM's display port carries "hdr_follow": true, and the guest's display
agent runs that output at 8-bit sRGB while no window there is in full
screen and at today's 10-bit PQ while one is (omacvm-displays,
omacvm-display-sync). The frames carry their colour in their depth (an
8-bit scanout is sRGB, a 10-bit one PQ, as before), so QEMU tags each one
right and the layer has EDR only for PQ. While the frames are 8-bit the
guest is told the headroom the display had while PQ showed (else its
most, capped at 16), not the ~1 the panel falls to, so its PQ rule is
ready for the next full screen; after the frames turn PQ, not less until
macOS's ramp is done (3 s; ui/omacvm-hdr-follow.h). Off: the layout and
the headroom are as before. qemu.log: "cocoa: HDR in full screen only:
on (...)|off (HDR as before)" when it changes, and once a minute the
number of SDR <-> PQ switches while it is on and there were some.

Why: an SDR desktop is the HDR-off path: 8-bit surfaces, no EDR, Chrome
draws 8-bit without its FP16 layer. HDR costs battery while nothing HDR is
on screen (the user's M1 Max: 2-3x less battery than macOS). Linux gives
no per-frame HDR signal under an SDR desktop, so full screen is the
trigger (ADR 0074).

Threads: the switch is read and watched on the main thread; QEMU's thread
publishes after each frame's alloc whether the surfaces show PQ and since
when (qatomic); the main thread's once-a-second look reads that for the
headroom. The held value is the main thread's only.

Upstream: OmacVM only (OmacVM's display port).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-hdr-follow.sh (rules and wiring);
src/app/guest/tests/test_omacvm_displays.py and test_display_sync.py (the
guest's side).

Applies after omacvm-cocoa-present-depth-hold.patch.

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
